l","tlr":"not_legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{2}{W}{W}","name":"Wrath of God","oracle_id":"34515b16-c9a4-4f98-8c77-416a7a523407","oracle_text":"Destroy all creatures. They can't be regenerated.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2023-08-04","toughness":null,"type_line":"Sorcery"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"If the target card is no longer in the graveyard when Cremate tries to resolve, it won't resolve and none of its effects will happen. You won't draw a card.","oracle_id":"c6a2e410-b182-48d1-aeb2-bc8de27e9cd2","published_at":"2012-10-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You must be able to target a card in a graveyard to cast Cremate.","oracle_id":"c6a2e410-b182-48d1-aeb2-bc8de27e9cd2","published_at":"2012-10-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"A permanent card is an artifact, creature, enchantment, land, or planeswalker card.","oracle_id":"f6ed46e2-08f9-4e89-aae3-e5dd7f30f007","published_at":"2025-10-02","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you return an Aura this way, you choose what the Aura will enchant just before it enters, but you can't choose any permanent cards that will enter at the same time as that Aura. An Aura returning to the battlefield this way doesn't target the player or permanent it will enchant, so permanents or players with hexproof may be chosen; however, the chosen recipient must be able to legally be enchanted by the Aura, so a player or permanent with protection from one of the Aura's qualities can't be chosen this way. If there's nothing legal for the Aura to enchant, it stays in the graveyard.","oracle_id":"f6ed46e2-08f9-4e89-aae3-e5dd7f30f007","published_at":"2025-10-02","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Permanent spells that were countered earlier in the turn never entered the battlefield, so they won't be legal targets for Brought Back.","oracle_id":"f6ed46e2-08f9-4e89-aae3-e5dd7f30f007","published_at":"2025-10-02","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
